---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { analytics, repo } from '../site'
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy — TabCabin"
  description="TabCabin keeps your data in your browser and sends it to the sync server only when you sign in. No analytics, no ads, no tracking."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <article class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-ink-2 [&_a]:font-medium [&_a]:text-accent-ink [&_a:hover]:underline [&_h2]:mt-12 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-[22px] [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-[-0.02em] [&_h2]:text-ink [&_li]:mt-1.5 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6">
      <h1 class="text-[38px] leading-tight font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[46px]">
        Privacy policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-ink-3">Last updated: October 2026</p>

      <p>
        TabCabin is an open-source browser extension and an optional sync server. This policy
        explains what happens with your data. In short: it stays with you, and it only travels to
        sync your own computers when you sign in.
      </p>

      <h2>What the extension stores</h2>
      <p>
        The things you save — page titles and addresses, notes, to-dos, images, reminders — and your
        settings are stored in your browser's local storage (IndexedDB). They never leave your
        browser unless you sign in to sync them.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      {analytics ? (
        <p>
          Nothing through the extension: it has no analytics, no advertising, no tracking and no
          crash reporting. This website counts visits, see below.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          Nothing. TabCabin has no analytics, no advertising, no tracking and no crash reporting.
        </p>
      )}
      <ul>
        <li>We do not sell, share or transfer any data to third parties.</li>
        <li>Without signing in there is no account and nothing is sent to any server.</li>
        <li>Your data is not used for any purpose other than showing your boards to you.</li>
      </ul>

      {analytics && (
        <>
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>
            The website counts visits with Umami, without cookies and without personal data. It
            records the page, the site that sent you here, your browser, system, device type, screen
            size, language and country, and keeps no IP addresses or anything else that identifies
            you. When your browser sends “Do Not Track”, nothing is counted.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      <h2>Network requests</h2>
      <p>
        To show what you saved, the extension loads website icons and images from the websites they
        belong to. Website icons are taken from the browser's own icon cache when possible. No other
        requests are made, except to the sync server once you sign in, and to your saved pages if
        you turn on link checks.
      </p>
      <p>
        Link checks are off until you turn them on in Settings. Then, about once a week, your
        browser asks each saved page whether it still loads, without cookies, and marks the ones
        that do not. The requests go straight to those websites; the results stay on your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        On a template page of this website, “Add to TabCabin” asks the installed extension to add
        that template. The page sends only the template's name and learns only that TabCabin is
        installed; your boards never go to the website. No other website can talk to the extension.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Tabs and tab groups</strong> — to list your open tabs, save the ones you choose
          and count how many you close each day (only the number, never which pages).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Context menus, active tab and scripting</strong> — to save the page you are on,
          only after you click the menu, the toolbar button or the shortcut. The extension has no
          access to websites otherwise.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Storage</strong> — to keep your boards on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Alarms and notifications</strong> — to show reminders you set.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bookmarks and top sites</strong> (optional) — only when you search bookmarks or
          import them; read locally, never sent anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Identity</strong> (optional) — only when you choose “Continue with Google”, to
          open Google's sign-in window.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Access to all websites</strong> (optional) — only while link checks are on, to ask
          your saved pages whether they still load. Turning link checks off gives it back.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Optional sync</h2>
      <p>
        When you sign in, your boards are sent to the sync server this copy of TabCabin was built
        with, so your other computers can download them. The server stores your username (or, with
        Google sign-in, your e-mail address and Google account id), a scrypt hash of your password
        if you use one, hashed session tokens and the data you sync (your boards, and how many tabs
        you closed, links you saved and to-dos you finished each day) — nothing else, and it is
        never used for anything but syncing. Anyone can also run the server themselves and build the
        extension for it. You can sign out at any time; your data stays in the browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once signed in, you can share a group as a read-only link. Anyone with that link sees the
        group's title, links, notes and to-dos until you stop sharing it or delete the group. The
        page is kept out of search engines and loads nothing from anywhere else.
      </p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>In the extension: Settings → Data → Delete all data, or uninstall the extension.</li>
        <li>
          On the sync server: ask the person who runs it
          {repo && ' (open an issue in the repository for the official one)'} and your account and
          all of its data are deleted.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>TabCabin is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect any information.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      {repo ? (
        <p>
          If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page and in the{' '}
          <a href={repo}>project repository</a>.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page.</p>
      )}

      {repo && (
        <>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions are welcome as an issue in the{' '}
            <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>GitHub repository</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
